        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Linhai, Gongqingcheng, Taizhou, Zhejiang, Jiangxi, Lin River, China\n- People: Wu Jiaduo, Nicole Struse\n- Roles: county-level city, table tennis player\n- Events: establishment of Gongqingcheng, 2006 German double championship\n\nFacts:\n- Linhai is a county-level city in Taizhou, Zhejiang Province, on the banks of the Lin River in eastern China.\n- Wu Jiaduo was born on 19 September 1977 in Linhai, Zhejiang, China.\n- In 2006, Nicole Struse and Wu Jiaduo won the German double championship.\n- Gongqingcheng is a county-level city in northern Jiangxi province, China, and it was established on 10 September 2010.",
